From 115f9e3f982e7cf56d8db7b2ab698af87236861b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:12:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] spec: runtime switch for the DFlash encoder fusion
 (LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT), both injection paths kept, default LEGACY on
 this fork

Upstream 662a0b012 fused the DFlash encoder (fc + rms norm) into the K/V injection decode: one llama_decode per chunk instead of llama_encode -> device-to-host readback -> llama_decode. It left no way to measure itself except a revert-only second binary, which confounds the delta with build drift and ships nothing. This commit adds the switch, and both paths stay: graph<true>, the fused embd branch and the legacy host path.

- llama-cparams.h: dflash_fused_inject (C API default true, DELIBERATELY unchanged - see below)
- llama-context.{h,cpp}: set_dflash_fused_inject; decode() selects the embd batch width (encoder input width when fused, draft width when not); C API llama_set_dflash_fused_inject in llama-ext.h
- models/dflash.cpp graph<false> embd branch: input width and the in-graph fc + norm follow the flag; the K/V projection below is shared by both paths
- common/speculative.cpp draft-dflash: reads the env once in the ctor, calls the setter, sizes batch_inject for the chosen width, logs one receipt line; process() gathers into features_buf and runs the encode step on the legacy path, straight into batch_inject on the fused one

lane-225 R38 merge: the DEFAULT IS FLIPPED to the legacy path on this fork. The R18 kernel wave measured the fused path at -0.98% CI95 [-1.16%, -0.80%] on the seat DFlash2 decode cell, so the verdict is DOCUMENTED-TAKE and the fused path does not ship as the default here. LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT=1 restores upstream 662a0b012 behaviour on the same binary. The C API default in llama-cparams.h stays fused because the legacy shape is a CALLER contract (the caller must llama_encode the chunk first), so only common/speculative.cpp - which owns both halves - defaults it off. This divergence from the wave report section 5 text (which recorded the branch default, fused) is deliberate and is recorded in docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md. Caveat that travels with it: -0.98% is under this box's own decode build floor (R18 report section 3, inert controls reach +3.71%), so this is a conservative default, not a measured win.

Probe condition: none (host-side speculative path, backend-independent). Override: LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT=1. Generic path: legacy encode + decode.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-212 R18 kernel wave, candidate R15-C2 (Fable 5.1 MEDIUM, kernel-maker); upstream mechanism 662a0b012 (#27310)
Measured-effect: DOCUMENTED-TAKE. Seat DFlash2 decode -0.98% CI95 [-1.16%, -0.80%] fused vs legacy; U-IQ4XS +0.05% [-0.56%, +0.67%]; U-Q3KXL -0.87% [-2.50%, +0.77%]. The wave's INERT control on the same pair moved +3.71% [+0.80%, +6.61%] on decode, so none of these clears the build floor.
Cherry-picked-from: 8aa3ab0e999cdbd29b742e0d9510a52f62a600d9 (lane-212/r15c2-dflash-encoder-fusion-2026-09-06, b10819 base)
Lane: lane-225
Conflict-resolved: hand: R55 risk-5 - upstream fc343a84b (llama_batch_ext) removed decode's local n_embd selection; the fork switch is re-homed into llama_batch_ext_select_n_embd_inp (llama-batch.h/.cpp): DFlash takes n_embd_inp_enc only when cparams.dflash_fused_inject, else the draft width; default arg true keeps upstream test-batch-alloc semantics. Legacy batch_compat builds the ext batch per call, so the runtime flag set by speculative.cpp is read live
